    "q-46150": {
      "dom_id": "step-q46150",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The formula that relates the work $W$ applied to an object with mass $m$, distance $d$ and time $t$ is $W=\\frac{m{d}^{2}}{{t}^{2}}.$ What are the units of work in terms of base units?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the unit of work, we substitute the base units of mass, distance, and time into the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =\\frac{m{d}^{2}}{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the unit of work is $\\frac{\\text{kg}\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}}{{\\text{s}}^{2}}.$",
