    "q-105441": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105441",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "A car dealership with $7$ sellers sells $50$ cars in a month. The owner uses the formula\n\n$$\nN=\\frac{c}{s}\n$$\n\nto determine, on average, the number of cars sold by each seller, where $c$ is the total of cars sold, and $s$ is the total number of sellers.\n\nFind an appropriate measurement unit for $N.$",
      "worked_solution": "We are solving for measurement units, so we can ignore the quantities $50$ and $7.$ They do not matter if we are just solving for units.\n\nSince $c$ represents $\\text{cars}$ and $s$ represents $\\text{sellers},$ the appropriate measurement unit for $N=\\frac{c}{s}$ is $\\frac{\\text{cars}}{\\text{seller}}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
