    "q-46090": {
      "dom_id": "step-q46090",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "A printer prints $1\\,250$ letters in $60$ minutes. To determine the number of letters that the printer prints on average, the owner uses the formula\n\n$$\nN=\\frac{l}{t},\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the number of letters printed and $t$ the time in minutes.\n\nIn words, what is the appropriate measurement unit for $N?$",
      "worked_solution": "We are solving for measurement units, so we can ignore the quantities $1\\,250$ and $60.$ They do not matter, if we are just solving for units.\n\nSince $l$ represents $\\text{letters}$ and $t$ represents $\\text{minute},$ the appropriate measurement unit for $N=\\frac{l}{t}$ is $\\frac{\\text{letters}}{\\text{minute}}.$ In words, this is 'letters per minute'.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
